reated as safe for that party.", "Newest usable poll is 53 days old; polling uncertainty inflated."]}, "overview": "Utah's 1st District is an open seat after redistricting reshaped it into the state's most Democratic-leaning territory. Ben McAdams, a well-known moderate with prior statewide experience, faces Republican Riley Owen and several minor candidates. McAdams has raised nearly $3 million and benefits from about $2.7 million in outside support, while Owen has raised only a small fraction of that and is being heavily outspent.\n\nA September poll of likely voters showed McAdams leading by a wide margin, and prediction markets put his chances near 97-98 percent. Utah's electorate still leans Republican overall, which could temper the Democratic advantage, but the combination of structural lean, money, and market pricing makes this race solidly in McAdams's favor heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 26.0}, {